different forms ice can take!

 I have an interesting puzzle I've tried to find the answer to for
years somewhat related to this. I saw a referance in I believe
Jacob Bronowski's "The Ascent of man" about an unusual type of
Innuit sculpture. These were small objects, and were kept in bags
made of animal skins. The interesting part is this. The objects
were not meant to be seen! You were supposed to place your hands
thru openings at either end of the bag, the sculpture was in a
small bag in the center of the large one. The idea was these
objects were only meant to be felt! If anyone has further info on
this, particularly the Innuit word for these objects, I would be
deeply appreciative.

 My favorite Innuit word comes from the old hunting technique of
waiting over a seals breathing hole in the ice (alue) for it to
return. Nickpocktook- the long wait.....



